# Never publish the commercial ROM or save files to a public repo.
*.nds
*.gba
*.sav
*.dsv
*.gci
*.savestate
tmp-e2e/

# Ghidra reverse-engineering workspace: machine-local and large (install ~0.9 GB,
# projects, server logs). Keep the LEAP analysis out of this repo.
ghidra_12.1.4_PUBLIC/
ghidra_12.1.4_PUBLIC_*.zip
ghidra-projects/
ghidra-mcp/
ghidra-mcp-headless.*.log

# REA comparison (morluto/rea clone, benchmark project, run artifacts)
rea/
ghidra-bench/
gmb.*.log
rea-*.json
rea-*.png

# Decompilation run: analysis logs, the export itself, and script build output
leap-decompiled/
leap-decomp-test/
leap-*.log
watch.*.log
ghidra-scripts/_build/
gl.*.log

# Vendored LEAP installer (196 MB). The ignore that covered this in the source repo
# did not travel with the copy, so it has to be excluded here. leap-decompiled/ itself
# is also deliberately not committed: 136 MB of generated output, reproducible from the
# analysed project with ghidra-scripts/DecompileAll.java.
leap/vendor/

# Reverse-engineering debug output
leap-decompiled-retry/
jstack-*.txt
gx.*.log
gx*.log
# General net for the run logs this work produces (verify.out.log, gxA.err.log, ...);
# the named patterns above kept missing a new family.
*.out.log
*.err.log
leap-year-verification.png
# Dynamic-probe artifacts from the TestLEAP format work (regenerated by the
# commands recorded in leap-year-verification.html)
_leap_probe*/
_leap_probe*.leap
_testleap_probe.txt
testleap.run.*.txt
_ext_*/
_ext_*.leap
_mx_*/
_mx_*.leap
_fm*/
_fm*.leap
# Going forward, dynamic probes belong under this single ignored directory so a new
# probe family cannot leak into a commit the way _ext_/_mx_/_fm_ did.
_probes/
.venv-frida/
# Rust build output for the headless LEAP port crate.
leap-rs/target/
__pycache__/
.commit-msg.tmp
leap-rs/target-*/
